The Grok CLI reader's Grok 1.0 usage.json ledger fallback — preferring the ACP
stream's turn_completed usage and consulting the per-session ledger only when
the stream carries none so a session reporting both is never counted twice,
pairing the timestamp-less ledger turns with the stream's turn_completed order,
folding the ledger's cacheCreationTokens into input because Grok publishes no
separate cache-write rate, and attributing the ledger's modelUsage entries per
model — together with the two silent-empty format sentinels (a Cursor export
header check that turns an unrecognised header into a skipped run with a
warning instead of an empty snapshot, and a Grok signals.json canary that warns
when a session reports completed turns and models used without any readable
usage) is adapted from upstream commit
b4a38745785a243ea23f5130285d78624f89a9f5 (2026-09-20) and re-expressed in this
repository's five-field mutually-exclusive token contract, KBU_USAGE_* root
resolution, and English parser warnings carried through the shared snapshot
collector's existing skipped/warnings fields.

The adapted code has since been substantially modified for this project,
